  Slug: interrogation-methodology
  DisplayName: Interrogation Methodology
  IconPath: icons/sundries/scrolls/scroll-writing-brown-grey.webp
  Description: People can't help but trust you, whether through your inherent likableness
    or your firm insistence on sticking to the truth. You have a way about you that
    gets others talking, and you've developed interrogative techniques to help you
    get to the truth of your investigations. You are trained in Diplomacy. You gain
    the No Cause for Alarm skill feat. You can also Pursue a Lead at the same time
    you @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Make an Impression], as long as you
    ask a question related to the creature with which you're conversing or a topic
    of your conversation. You also gain the Pointed Question action.
